Z||000000||DJRice||02-14-2001||11:15 PM||||Included in todays pile of junkmail is a preapproved credit app from one of those companies offering a Credit Card with the "32K chip Smart Cards".  It claims to have "advanced digital security" and offers a "smart card reader" for "advanced security" and "convienient checkout" with websites.  <P>Is anybody else using one of these things yet?  Is it really that much easier and more conveinient?  Are these people using these cards to more closely monitor my spending habits (kinda like cuecat)?  Should I sign up for it just because there is no annual fee and it looks cool?<P>Thoughts anyone?<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||5
Z||000001||RNGCRSH||02-14-2001||11:50 PM||||I like the way they say "advanced security".<P>I wonder how much it would help when someone steals your number and uses it online or the phone for purchases.<P>sounds more like hype to get you to switch.<P>the convenient checkout might work like the Mobil speedpass or something like that, but it seems like convenience would cancle security and vice versa.<P>I just stick with the card that gives me the most back on purchases. I have a Dell Visa card and earn 1% on purchases. It adds up at 3~4K per month of spending. Buying a new dell system soon at a $700 discount.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroLisa||02-15-2001||01:55 PM||||I have an american express blue, and I think it's got that chip in it...don't know much about it, just that it looks purdy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>(and no i didnt get it for that reason, my mom got it for me)<BR>Lisa||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||02-15-2001||04:20 PM||||I have a regular old Visa card.. most basic one I could get.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Sure, I like my privacy.. but do I really care that people find out I buy sci-fi books online from Barnes & Noble, order parts from allelectronics.com, trance CDs from Sunrise records and car magazines from the college bookstore?? big deal.. I like the idea of content-related advertising, I'd rather see that than ads and products geared to things I have no interest in.<BR>so hey, if a company wants to watch my spending habits and realizes I like Star Wars books, DJ Tiesto CDs and magazines about street rods, astronomy and car audio... good for them.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>My concerns about privacy are that all email is monitored, as well as cell phone calls, etc. by the NSA.. I don't trust them at all.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||02-15-2001||09:16 PM||||Our school uses ID cards with the smart chip in them. We can also load money onto them via our bank cards and use them all over the city at stores , vending machines , the bus taxi's ..ect. There called Visa Cash cards. The chip is easy to remove , and from what I have seen easy to reprogram using a card reader they hand out. It's the size of a Keychain and you plug the card into it. The LCD read out gives the amount of money remaining on the card.<P>JM||||reg||1
